+# Full study: Arxiv.id2303_01089.conjecture_1_4
+
+## Frozen object
+
+This target is the exact `conjecture_1_4` declaration from the pinned
+`formal-conjectures-2270d31e` revision `2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669`,
+located at `FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2303.01089/FurstenbergTimesPTimesQ.lean:84-96`.
+The provider census contains `sorryAx`; its bytes are statement provenance only.
+
+```lean
+theorem conjecture_1_4 :
+    answer(False) ↔
+      ∀ p q : ℕ, 2 <= p → 2 <= q → MultiplicativelyIndependent p q →
+        ∀ μ : ProbabilityMeasure 𝕋,
+          MeasureTheory.IsAtomLess μ.1 → MeasurePreserving (Tn p) μ μ →
+          Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => μ.map (Tn_continuous (q ^ n)).aemeasurable) atTop
+            (𝓝 UnitAddCircle.ProbabilityMeasure)
+```
+
+The source uses `answer(False)`, which reduces to `False` in the pinned utility. The local
+statement keeps the source definitions in a target namespace and replays the closed
+proposition without importing the provider theorem.
+
+## Mathematical context
+
+Badea–Grivaux’s paper (Discrete Analysis 2024:10, arXiv:2303.01089v3) states Conjecture
+1.4 for an atomless `T_p`-invariant probability measure and says that `T_{q^n} μ` should
+converge weak-star to normalized Lebesgue measure. Their Theorem 1.5 proves a residual
+family with large Fourier coefficients along `q^n`, so convergence fails generically.
+This human disproof boundary is not a local formal proof.
+
+## Resolution frontier
+
+The source statement, local notation, closed-root transport, and exact shape of a
+refutation witness elaborate at trust level 0. The missing root is a formal construction
+of an atomless `T_p`-invariant measure whose `T_{q^n}` pushforwards fail to converge. No
+claim-specific axiom or provider `sorryAx` body fills that cut.
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:BEGIN -->
+### PU-00 — exact frozen statement
+
+`Statement.lean` replays the source-side notation and defines `FrozenStatement` as the
+closed proposition obtained after `answer(False)` is normalized to `False`. `Target` is
+definitionally equal to that proposition; no provider theorem body is imported.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:BEGIN -->
+### PU-01 — convergence obligation
+
+The right-hand side quantifies `p` and `q` with lower bounds and multiplicative independence,
+then ranges over an atomless probability measure `μ` preserved by `Tn p`. The conclusion is
+Tendsto convergence of the pushforwards under `Tn (q ^ n)` to `UnitAddCircle.ProbabilityMeasure`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:BEGIN -->
+### PU-02 — bidirectional statement transport
+
+`frozen_to_target` and `target_to_frozen` are definitional identity transports. The source
+aliases are checked too, so notation and the closed-root boundary cannot drift during a
+future proof replacement.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:BEGIN -->
+### PU-03 — formal refutation witness shape
+
+`RefutationWitness` packages natural numbers `p,q`, an atomless probability measure,
+`Tn p`-preservation, and the negation of the required `Tn (q^n)` convergence. This is the
+exact datum needed to discharge the right-to-left implication.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:BEGIN -->
+### PU-04 — conditional root theorem
+
+`target_of_refutation` proves `Target` from a supplied `RefutationWitness`, and
+`refutation_root_shape` exposes that implication. The analytic construction of such a
+witness is deliberately not asserted: it is the open machine cut.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:BEGIN -->
+### PU-05 — human disproof boundary
+
+Badea–Grivaux, *Around Furstenberg’s Times p, Times q Conjecture*, Theorem 1.5, proves a
+residual family of continuous `T_p`-invariant measures with large Fourier coefficients along
+`q^n`, hence failure of convergence to normalized Lebesgue measure. This is mathematical
+evidence, not a kernel-checked Lean proof.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:BEGIN -->
+### PU-06 — trust and composition frontier
+
+The local audit reports only ordinary transitive Mathlib foundations and no `sorryAx`,
+unsafe declaration, claim-specific axiom, or bodyless oracle. A formalization of the paper’s
+Baire/Fourier construction can later compose the typed cut; this package stops here.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:BEGIN -->
+### PU-ROOT-OPEN — provisional handoff
+
+The exact trust-zero counterexample witness and analytic proof are absent. Therefore
+`machine_complete` and `theorem_complete` remain false. Identity, transport, readable
+coverage, and structural replay are complete and handed to the independent Master.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:END -->
+
+## Conclusion
+
+Identity exactness, statement transport, readable reconstruction, and structural validation
+are closed. This is a truthful provisional nonacceptance handoff: `readable_complete=true`,
+while `machine_complete=false` and `theorem_complete=false` until the analytic refutation
+is formalized and independently accepted.
